    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16A Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-16a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, from\n3 consecutive meetings of the Commission; or\n\n(c) the Commissioner fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 16B.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, from\n3 consecutive meetings of the Commission; or\n\n(c) the Commissioner fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 16B.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1af6546737d55f00b015037b2ce418054eacfdbaafcc9b6c731018cfbdb2873b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16A Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n\n(2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a\nCommissioner if:\n\n(a) the Commissioner:\n\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or\n\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of his or her creditors; or\n\n(b) the Commissioner is absent, except on leave of absence, from\n3 consecutive meetings of the Commission; or\n\n(c) the Commissioner fails, without reasonable excuse, to\ncomply with section 16B."
    },
