    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-19a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19A Remuneration and allowances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-19a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n12            Australian Centre for International Agricultural Research Amendment Act 2007       No.\n115, 2007\nno determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in\noperation, the appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the allowances\nthat are prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n12            Australian Centre for International Agricultural Research Amendment Act 2007       No.\n115, 2007\nno determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in\noperation, the appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the allowances\nthat are prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-19a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-19a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-19a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "060208f53addd92d8e52f2cd743de70380df4f75599d115d1ef8a0e6a2118db1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-19a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19A Remuneration and allowances",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n12            Australian Centre for International Agricultural Research Amendment Act 2007       No.\n115, 2007\nno determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in\noperation, the appointed member of the Council is to be paid the\nremuneration that is prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(2) An appointed member of the Council is to be paid the allowances\nthat are prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973."
    },
