    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Acting CEO",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may appoint a person to act as the CEO:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the CEO (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the CEO is\nabsent from duty or from Australia, or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nSection 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contains provisions\nrelating to acting appointments.\n\n(2) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act under\nan appointment is not invalid merely because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect; or\n\n(d) the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may appoint a person to act as the CEO:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the CEO (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the CEO is\nabsent from duty or from Australia, or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nSection 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contains provisions\nrelating to acting appointments.\n\n(2) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act under\nan appointment is not invalid merely because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect; or\n\n(d) the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-29-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9d410d0124edeba19dead3e71f1316b123d3628b6f079fac6c156fc07b65bd4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-1-sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Acting CEO",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may appoint a person to act as the CEO:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of the CEO (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the CEO is\nabsent from duty or from Australia, or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nSection 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contains provisions\nrelating to acting appointments.\n\n(2) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act under\nan appointment is not invalid merely because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect; or\n\n(d) the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased."
    },
