      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-2-sec-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-2-sec-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "In this Schedule:\namend includes repeal and remake.\nasset means:\n\n(a) any legal or equitable estate or interest in real or personal\nproperty, whether actual, contingent or prospective; or\n\n(b) any right, power, privilege or immunity, whether actual,\ncontingent or prospective.\nassets official, in relation to an asset other than land, means the person\nor authority who, under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, under a trust instrument or otherwise, has responsibility for\nkeeping a register in relation to assets of the kind concerned.\nBoard has the same meaning as in the old law.\nCentre means the Australian Centre for International Agricultural\nResearch established by the Australian Centre for International\nAgricultural Research Act 1982.\nCEO means the Chief Executive Officer of the Centre.\ncommencement time means the time when this Schedule commences.\nCommission has the same meaning as in the new law.\nDirector has the same meaning as in the old law.\ninstrument:\n\n(a) includes:\n\n(i) a contract, deed, undertaking or agreement; and\n\n(ii) a notice, authority, order or instruction; and\n\n(iii) an instrument made under an Act or regulations; and\n\n(iv) regulations; but\n\n(b) does not include an Act.\nland means any legal or equitable estate or interest in real property,\nwhether actual, contingent or prospective.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 2\nPreliminary  Part 1",
      "skos:definition": "In this Schedule:\namend includes repeal and remake.\nasset means:\n\n(a) any legal or equitable estate or interest in real or personal\nproperty, whether actual, contingent or prospective; or\n\n(b) any right, power, privilege or immunity, whether actual,\ncontingent or prospective.\nassets official, in relation to an asset other than land, means the person\nor authority who, under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, under a trust instrument or otherwise, has responsibility for\nkeeping a register in relation to assets of the kind concerned.\nBoard has the same meaning as in the old law.\nCentre means the Australian Centre for International Agricultural\nResearch established by the Australian Centre for International\nAgricultural Research Act 1982.\nCEO means the Chief Executive Officer of the Centre.\ncommencement time means the time when this Schedule commences.\nCommission has the same meaning as in the new law.\nDirector has the same meaning as in the old law.\ninstrument:\n\n(a) includes:\n\n(i) a contract, deed, undertaking or agreement; and\n\n(ii) a notice, authority, order or instruction; and\n\n(iii) an instrument made under an Act or regulations; and\n\n(iv) regulations; but\n\n(b) does not include an Act.\nland means any legal or equitable estate or interest in real property,\nwhether actual, contingent or prospective.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 2\nPreliminary  Part 1",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-2-sec-1-norm"
        },
        {
