    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Constitutional safety net—acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-2-sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of compensation to\nthe person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n(3)\nIn this item:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi)\nof the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of compensation to\nthe person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n(3)\nIn this item:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi)\nof the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-2-sec-16-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-2-sec-16-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e12c31517b006efceb0092119a9c451ccfb0f69732f1b5f727294db086c4685d",
      "skos:note": "Compensation for acquisition of property without just terms"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007#sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Constitutional safety net—acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of compensation to\nthe person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n(3)\nIn this item:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi)\nof the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution."
    },
    {
